Hi Mike,

thank you for developing the micro_era5 function. I just wondered: have you run comparisons with the micro_ncep data yet??
I looked at the intercomparison project WRIT: Monthly Timeseries: NOAA Physical Sciences Laboratory <https://psl.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/data/testdap/timeseries.pl> and plotted monthly time series in a few locations. They seemed quite different, the era5 data being much smoother than the ncep ones (at least in these specific locations). Correlations ranging from .3 to .5 depending on the parameters.
But I haven't tried to see how the results of the microclimate model were affected by the use of one or the other yet. Has anyone looked into that?

Cheers,
Claire

